*.local.md

# AUDIT-04-F14: scratch directories some tooling drops in the repo root. Three
# empty ones (tmp87t30pr_, tmp89wr1inc, tmps_49bgvy) sat here from 2026-07-28
# and were invisible to `git status` only because git does not track empty
# directories -- a non-empty one would have read as session work.
tmp*/

# OPS-07: machine-generated local tooling state (finding ledger, hook state,
# run history). Session-scoped and per-developer — not project content. It was
# inherited as an untracked path across three sessions before being decided.
.mimosa/

# AUDIT-08 production-release hygiene. {"_tag":"Error","error":{"code":"LegacyProjectNotLinkedError","message":"Cannot find project ref. Have you run supabase link?"}} writes to the
# CURRENT directory, so a release run from the repo root drops production
# roles/schema/DATA here as untracked files -- one `git add -A` from being
# committed. That happened on 2026-08-10: a 172 KB production data.sql sat in
# the repo root. The runbook says to write dumps OUTSIDE the repository
# (supabase/deploy/PENDING-2026-08-10-production-migration-runbook.md step 4);
# this is the backstop for when someone runs the command from here anyway.
# Anchored to the ROOT so a legitimately tracked schema.sql elsewhere is
# unaffected.
/roles.sql
/schema.sql
/data.sql
/*.dump

# K4-PORT-02 (D300): local statutory SOURCE ARTIFACTS, deliberately untracked.
#
# `.sources/statutory/` holds the official PDFs a session quotes statute from
# (the enacted Income-tax Act 2025, the ICAI editions carrying the Finance Act
# 2026 and the Income-tax Rules 2026, CBDT memoranda). They live in the project
# so they stop living in `~/Downloads`, which is the OWNER'S PERSONAL DIRECTORY
# and a transient one -- `K4-PORT-00` opened an unlabeled PDF there expecting
# statute and found an owner personal record.
#
# They are NOT COMMITTED, and that is the established convention rather than an
# oversight: this repository tracks ZERO PDFs, `K4-PORT-00-S2`'s 106 MB Act PDF
# was registered in the source register without being vendored, and these four
# artifacts total ~134 MB against a 39 MB `.git`. Committing them would more
# than quadruple the repository permanently, since git history cannot be pruned
# cheaply.
#
# What IS committed is the evidence that makes them verifiable and replaceable:
# `docs/evidence/statutory-sources/manifest.json` (SHA-256 + provenance per
# artifact) and the source-register entries in
# `docs/operations/official-source-retrieval.md` §6. A session that finds a file
# missing re-retrieves it from the registered URL and checks the hash.
/.sources/
